id: pm-gh1729
title: "GH-1729: the extension test harness passes a compact output_format receipt that the native CLI refuses with extension_read_output_invalid since 2026.11.13"
description: "GH-1729 (filed 2026-11-14, reproduced on the 2026.11.7, 2026.11.13 and 2026.11.14 artifacts). An extension command declares read_output { row_keys: [\"rows\"] } and an output_format service returns a compact receipt ({ ok: true, output: \"receipt.md\" }). The native CLI on 2026.11.13 and 2026.11.14 refuses the receipt-only handler result with exit 2 and extension_read_output_invalid before the formatter receipt, while the same result with a rows array passes. createExtensionTestHarness().runCommand() handles both, so a package author cannot detect the native refusal before adoption; 2026.11.7 accepted both. Expected from the issue: make native output admission testable through the public harness, or document that the harness validates only the handler result and requires a packed native probe; if declared row keys are intentionally mandatory before custom formatting, document the compatible compact receipt pattern and migration. Malformed and oversized output must stay refused. Duplicate check: searched extension read_output row_keys output_format receipt harness native refusal; no open item."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[5]: extensions,"gh:1729",read-output,sdk,testing
created_at: "2026-11-14T15:21:20.930Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-14T20:53:38.046Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-14T19:16:40.530Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-14T19:16:40.530Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 150
acceptance_criteria: "A regression fixture distinguishes receipt-only output, valid rows with compact formatter output, malformed rows and oversized delivered output across the native CLI and the test harness; Package authors can detect the native refusal before adoption, either through the harness or a documented packed-native probe; Valid compact output stays compact and malformed or oversized output stays refused"
parent: pm-ugqx
risk: medium
confidence: medium
reporter: unbraind
severity: medium
resolution: "assertExtensionReadOutputResult (src/sdk/read-output/extension.ts) is the shared admission; runRegisteredCommandForTest (src/sdk/testing.ts) applies it to every handled result of a command whose last registration declares read_output, after a registered command-result override, skipping suppressed host output, and to a structured output_format replacement (the activation attaches its service registry; the service payload mirrors native resolveOutputService with merged output controls and resolvedOutputFormat). The refusal carries required/why text naming the compact-receipt pattern; docs/SDK.md documents it."
expected_result: Receipt-only and malformed results are refused in the harness exactly as natively; valid rows with a compact formatter receipt pass both; oversized delivered output stays refused natively
actual_result: "direct-caller-option-contract.integration.spec covers receipt-only, rows, empty rows, malformed and oversized cases across the built CLI and the harness; harness-parity.spec covers overrides, suppression, structured and string services and explicit encodings; linked run passed 34/34"
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-gh1726,related,"2026-11-14T15:26:13.918Z","harness:claude-code","cli:update:dep",detected
comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-14T16:56:07.237Z","harness:claude-code","Root cause (2026-11-14): attachExtensionReadOutputRows (src/sdk/read-output/extension.ts) refuses a result that lacks a declared row collection before projection or any output_format service runs, which is intended: declared row_keys are a promise. runRegisteredCommandForTest never ran that check, so a receipt-only handler passed package tests and failed natively. Fix: the check is extracted as assertExtensionReadOutputResult and the harness applies it to every handled result of a command whose last registration declares read_output, so package tests now fail with the same code and message. The refusal now also carries required/why text naming the compatible pattern: keep returning the rows (an empty collection is valid) and let the output_format service render the compact receipt. Oversized delivered output stays refused natively (output_budget_exceeded) even with valid rows; the regression fixture covers receipt-only, rows, empty rows, malformed rows and oversized delivery."
  "2026-11-14T19:02:15.162Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review round 4 (head 66ec6d502), one P2 finding, verified and fixed: the harness ignored an outputFormat passed through global options when it chose the output_format branch, while native formatEffectiveOutput merges the global output controls (outputInclude, outputLimit, outputBudget, outputFormat, outputSession, outputCursor, outputRowContract) over the command options before resolveReadOutputEncoding. The harness now merges the same keys first; harness-parity.spec covers command-option and global spellings."
  "2026-11-14T19:12:36.057Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review round 5 (head 6f1062e37), one P2 finding, verified and fixed: the harness resolved the encoding from the merged command and global output controls but then handed the output_format service the unmerged options, so a service reading payload.command_options.outputFormat saw undefined where native output passes toon. The payload now mirrors native resolveOutputService: command_options are the merged options plus resolvedOutputFormat, and payload.options/global carry command and commandOptions."
  "2026-11-14T19:40:39.235Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review round 6 (pushed head b52035aab, PR #1732), one P2 finding, verified and fixed: the harness formatter payload omitted the dispatch metadata native resolveOutputService passes in payload.options and payload.global (commandArgs, pmRoot); a formatter keyed on commandArgs[0] supplied rows natively but not in the harness. Both now carry command, commandArgs, pmRoot and the resolved commandOptions."
  "2026-11-14T20:53:38.045Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review round 7 (head 6c9fe839a), one P2 finding, verified and fixed: harness output hooks lacked the portable workspace coordinates (source_workspace_root, repo_root, pm_root_rel) that native runActiveCommandHandler resolves with resolvePortableWorkspaceContext, so a service keyed on them supplied rows natively but not in the harness. The harness now resolves them into the handler context (as native dispatch does for the handler too), and the command-result override and output_format service inherit them."
